# Dryas Workflow
- Read `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-workflow.md` before multi-step work or when asked about the workflow (machine notes, if present: `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-local.md`).
- The repo is the source of truth for these rules and that doc. Edit the repo (`claude/CLAUDE.md.template`, `docs/workflow.md`), merge, then re-run setup (`install/install.sh`, once per Claude config dir). Never hand-edit the plugin files, the copy in `~/.dryas/docs`, or these injected rules.

# Workflow rules
- Brainstorm first, always (dryas:brainstorm); build or dispatch only after the user approves the design.
- Design work (UI/UX, layout, visual style, components, on-screen copy): run `dryas:lens` (design panel: craft, `impeccable`, `ui-ux-pro-max`); its result is an Artifact page. New features: product panel (focus, craft, data) in brainstorm, or when the user says "3 lens".
- Reverse-engineering work (software without source): use REA, on demand (`dryas rea on`, then restart; never `rea setup`); brainstorm says when, the user can decline.
- Single-file fix: plain Claude on the strong tier. Multi-step: `/orchestrate <task>` on the approved design.
- Every multi-step task runs in its own git worktree. One agent per worktree: never two sessions in one worktree; parallel loops each get their own worktree and branch. Merge after `/wreview` and dryas:verify.
- Layers: Jev decides (gates, routing; local judge or Jev model) and never writes code or plans; Dryas memory learns; Dryas skills are the process. Superpowers and Ruflo are optional extras; name the Dryas skills even when they are installed.
- Hook order per event: scope lock -> gate -> memory -> observer (observe-only, last). Stages: `jev/chain.json` in the Dryas plugin folder.
- `.orchestrate/` (incl. `.orchestrate/PLAN.md`) in a worktree is scratch: git-ignored, never committed.
- Ask before any install, move, delete or overwrite, including any change to the account's settings.json (`$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json`, default `~/.claude/settings.json`). Show a dry-run or diff first.
- Commands: `/orchestrate`, `/wplan`, `/wreview`, `/commit` (Jev-gated, never pushes), `/tune` (weekly calibration), `/retro` (lessons from a finished task), `/handoff` (Jev-scored reset: run it, then `/clear`; `/handoff move` to switch accounts).
- Nobody is prompted during /orchestrate: hooks decide or the orchestrator does; what needs the user waits for the end report.
- Never ship a release worse than the last (prompts per task, speed, cost vs the previous release; tools/compare_v1.py).
